{red|**Describe your reaction to your ex moving on.**

How did you find out?}{red| What emotions hit you?}{red| What was the intensity?}{red| What thoughts have been cycling through your mind?}{red| How has it affected your daily life and functioning?}

Write about your reaction:

{red|**When you find out they have moved on, you do not feel one thing.** You feel everything.

**Jealousy burns first.** You see them with someone new and something animal wakes up. This is my territory. Except it is not anymore.

**Then anger.** How dare they be happy?}{red| How dare they find someone while you are still picking up pieces?}{red| They caused this wreckage and now they get to walk away into someone else's arms?}

{red|**Underneath the anger, sadness.** This is really over. Whatever hope you were secretly holding, however small, is gone now. The door is not just closed. It is bricked over.

**Fear creeps in.** What if they were right?}{red| What if you are unlovable?}{red| What if they find happiness and you spend the rest of your life alone?}

{red|**Shame, too.** You should be over this. It has been months, or years. What is wrong with you that this still has power?}

**And loneliness.** Because now you know they have someone, and you do not, and the contrast is unbearable.

**All of this.** At once. Crashing in waves. No wonder you feel like you are drowning.

{red|**Be honest about the destructive urges you are experiencing.**

What behaviors have you engaged in that made things worse: social media stalking, contact, bad-mouthing?}

{red|What urges are you currently fighting?}{red| What triggers these urges?}{red| What has been the result when you have given in?}

Write about your destructive urges:

{red|**Create a plan to resist destructive behaviors.**

Social media: What steps will I take to stop checking?}{red| Will I block or unfollow?}

{red|Contact: What will I do when I am tempted to reach out?}

{red|Accountability: Who will I tell about my urges to help me stay strong?}

{red|Replacement: What will I do instead when urges hit?}

Write your resistance plan:

{red|**Reflect on how your ex's timeline has affected you.**

Have you felt behind or like you are losing a race?}{red| Has their quick move-on made you doubt your own progress?}{red| Have you been tempted to rush into something just to catch up?}{red| What would it mean to fully honor your own pace?}

Write about your timeline feelings:

{red|**Identify the false conclusions your mind has been generating.**

What painful interpretations have you been making about your ex's new relationship?}

{red|**For each one, write a truer counter-statement.**

Which lie has been most destructive for you?}

Write your false conclusions and counter-truths:

{red|**Reflect on the timeline of your ex's new relationship.**

How quickly did they move on?}{red| Do you have reason to believe there was overlap with your marriage?}{red| What questions does their speed raise for you?}{red| What specific pain does the rapid transition cause?}

Write about your experience of their speed:

{red|**Reflect on how your ex's new relationship affects your children and your feelings about it.**

What are your concerns about your children and the new partner?}{red| How have your children responded to the new partner?}{red| What has been hardest for you about this situation?}{red| How have you been handling it with your kids?}

Write about your children-related concerns:

{red|**Honestly assess where your attention has been going.**

How much mental energy have you been spending on your ex's new relationship?}{red| What areas of your own life have been neglected while you focused on them?}{red| What would you like to invest your attention in instead?}{red| What would change if you fully shifted your focus to your own life?}

Write your attention audit:

{red|**Assess your current peace in relation to your ex.**

How much does your emotional state depend on what they are doing?}{red| What would it take for you to have peace regardless of their choices?}{red| What internal sources of peace do you have access to?}{red| What practices help you find calm when thoughts of them arise?}

Write your peace assessment:

{red|What is the most important thing you have learned through this journey about handling your ex moving on?}

{red|What do you want to remember when the pain resurfaces?}

Write your key insight:

{red|What commitments will you make going forward?}

{red|How will you handle difficult emotions when they arise?}{red| How will you avoid destructive behaviors?}{red| How will you focus on your own life?}{red| How will you cultivate peace independent of your ex?}

